#
# Firing fixture for the cross-node-glut meta-rule. Two DIFFERENT-code findings at
# ONE non-trivial gmeow:findingAnchor whose logic:FindingCategory polarities OPPOSE:
# ex:glutSupported carries logic:FindingContradictionWitness (gmeow:categoryPolarity
# logic:InfoSupported) and ex:glutOpposed carries logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict
# (gmeow:categoryPolarity logic:InfoOpposed). The anchor is typed gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor
# (the projection's guard for a real source position), so the rule must derive
# gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith between them — the Supported/Opposed coherence clash the
# same-fingerprint merge cannot see across codes. The gmeow:categoryPolarity wiring
# is read from diagnostics/module.ttl by the harness. Consumed ONLY by
# crates/conformance/tests/diagnostics_meta_findings.rs; lives under tests/ so the
# global make validate gate never loads it as data.
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/diagnostics/tests/> .

ex:glutAnchor a gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor .

ex:glutSupported
    a gmeow:Finding ;
    gmeow:findingAnchor ex:glutAnchor ;
    gmeow:findingCategory logic:FindingContradictionWitness .

ex:glutOpposed
    a gmeow:Finding ;
    gmeow:findingAnchor ex:glutAnchor ;
    gmeow:findingCategory logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict .
